{
  "experiment_id": "9701014b-3418-46a2-acb4-d59f235388dc",
  "findings": [
    "The n=20 gate is a deliberately strong-effect kill test, not a sensitive moderate-effect estimation study.",
    "For a Holm-rank test needing >=16/20 positives, 80% marginal power requires q\u22480.8416 and 90% requires q\u22480.8731 true family-level superiority.",
    "For a rank needing >=15/20, 80% marginal power requires q\u22480.7988 and 90% requires q\u22480.8342.",
    "Full four-test power cannot be identified without the joint dependence of the four sign statistics. Two anchors are reported: perfect positive correlation reduces the minimal gate to K>=16; independent test-count approximation requires all four >=15 and at least two >=16. Neither is asserted as truth.",
    "A valid v2.2 null should therefore weaken a large, broadly consistent single-site T1 mechanism, but it should not be phrased as high-powered evidence against moderate or heterogeneous plan-state effects.",
    "Because no outcomes have been seen, a larger confirmation cohort could still be preregistered prospectively if the scientific goal changes from strong-effect kill test to moderate-effect estimation. However changing n now would supersede v2.2 and incur additional compute; the current design is coherent if interpreted narrowly."
  ],
